node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
packages/web/dev-dist
*.log

# Tests never run inside the image, and the runtime stage COPIEs whole source directories
# (packages/api/src, packages/shared/src) — without this the test files that live next to those
# sources would ship to users. Keeping them out of the CONTEXT is what makes the runtime
# allowlist honest; `scripts/image-inventory.ts` asserts the result in the BUILT ARTEFACT,
# which is the load-bearing check (this file is easy to bypass by adding a differently-named
# file later).
#
# THE CONVENTION: a test-only module inside a shipped `src/` tree carries `.test` in its
# basename — `*.test.ts` for suites, `*.test-support.ts` for helpers, `*.test-child.ts` for the
# processes DB tests spawn. One glob then covers all of them. Do NOT invent a fourth spelling:
# `test-helpers.ts` and `testSupport.ts` used to exist, matched nothing, and shipped — including
# a module importing `fast-check`, which the production prune correctly removes, so users got an
# unloadable file.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.test-*.ts
**/*.test-*.tsx
packages/*/src/**/__fixtures__

# No dot-prefixed files or directories belong in the image (.git, env files,
# editor and agent scratch dirs). .gitignore does NOT apply to the Docker build
# context, so without this `COPY . .` would bake a maintainer's local working
# files into the image published to public GHCR. A CI build is clean (a tag
# checkout has no untracked files); this line guards the LOCAL `docker build`.
.*
CLAUDE.local.md
*.local.md
